## Added

- Seven Roslyn analyzers (CRSPEC0001–CRSPEC0007), bundled with `Cratis.Specifications`, `Cratis.Specifications.XUnit` and `Cratis.Specifications.NUnit`, that warn when:
  - a test method inside a specification is not named `should_*` (CRSPEC0001);
  - a file declares more than one specification (CRSPEC0002);
  - a `[Fact]`/`[Test]` is placed on a `given` context, where it never runs (CRSPEC0003);
  - a `should_*` method is missing its test attribute, so it never runs (CRSPEC0004);
  - a specification calls a base lifecycle method (`base.Establish()`/`Because()`/`Destroy()`) explicitly, running it twice (CRSPEC0005);
  - a specification that declares test methods is not `public`, so the runner skips it (CRSPEC0006);
  - the action under test (`Because`) is declared on a reusable `given` context (CRSPEC0007).
- Both xUnit (`[Fact]`/`[Theory]`) and NUnit (`[Test]`/`[TestCase]`) test attributes are recognized.

## Changed

- The packages now target `net8.0`, `net9.0` and `net10.0`, matching Arc and Chronicle.
- Updated `nunit` to 4.6.1, `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk` to 18.7.0, and `Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub` to 10.0.300.

## Fixed

- The build workflow now installs the .NET 8/9/10 SDKs (it previously pinned an SDK that could not satisfy the repository's .NET 10 requirement) and runs the analyzer specs in CI.

## Removed

- Dropped the `net48` target framework. Consumers on .NET Framework should remain on the previous release.

## Fixed

- Comments stay attached to their line during canonical printing and `expand-layout` for the remaining directive lines. These include:
  - enum values and concept reasons;
  - policy requirements and persona policies;
  - UI profile, theme and theme-compatibility lines;
  - contribution and screen-action labels and order;
  - implementation file references;
  - the scalar subdirectives in specifications, captures, projections and commands.

  The typed JSON syntax is unchanged.
- Comments on enum and other collection values follow their value when a syntax tree or workspace edit reorders, inserts or removes values.

## Changed

- A projection block that repeats `automap` or `no automap` reports `PLAY0452` (warning). The last setting still wins, and canonical printing keeps each line's comments.

Closes #281

## Added

- Stage renders more of the executable model onto Cratis now that the upstream fixes are released:
  - projection literal mappings in `from` blocks, using only literals Chronicle's fluent value expression can carry exactly;
  - removing a child through a join;
  - `$context.occurred` on produced events, with one timestamp for the payload and the event's occurrence;
  - contract and production tags that aren’t duplicated. This is part of #117.
- Validation rules and command requirements with warning or information severity reject the command, using Arc's `[BlockOnValidationSeverity]`. (#116)
- Specifications for protected queries run through Arc's query pipeline, including denials. They are admitted only when every seeded event comes from the queried key.
- The semantic runtime rebuilds its state from stored events on restart through Screenplay's `EstablishWorld`. It refuses to start on a history it can't reproduce.

## Changed

- Stage targets Chronicle 19.8.1, Arc 22.25.0 and Screenplay 4.41.1. Generated applications and the Host image use the same versions, and CI checks the Chronicle projection oracle against v19.8.1.
- The semantic engine no longer registers Chronicle projection mirrors, so its read models no longer appear as projection views in the Workbench. The admission endpoint no longer reports `projectionMirror`. The default engine is unchanged.
- Specifications that assert a value derived from `$context.occurred` are rejected, because the generated handler uses the actual time.

## Still rejected

These are still rejected, each with its STAGE diagnostic:
- composite-key read models, which need https://github.com/Cratis/Chronicle/issues/4265;
- `FromAll`, which needs https://github.com/Cratis/Chronicle/issues/4266;
- literals in `every`/`all` blocks;
- the projection shapes tracked in Chronicle #4125 and #4166;
- role-only policies (Arc #2761);
- per-run projection specifications (#15);
- given read models (#14).

Also part of #57, #23 and #15.
